@startuml
' Deployment diagram — where it runs
' Sources: ../../specification/01-architecture.md, ../../operations/deployment.md

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #333

node "The machine" as M {
  node "systemd --user" as SD {
    [mdview-reader.service] as SVC
  }
  node "Python 3" as PY {
    [server.py\n127.0.0.1:8765] as SRV
  }
  node "The browser" as BR {
    [Firefox\nthe extension, the tabs] as FF
    [Edge --app\nthe reader's window] as ED
  }
  node "The disk" as DISK {
    [the reader's roots] as ROOTS
    [~/mdview\nthe repository] as HOME
  }
  node "The internet" as NET {
    [api.dictionaryapi.dev] as D1
    [api.datamuse.com] as D2
    [en.wiktionary.org] as D3
  }
}

SVC --> SRV : starts and restarts it
SRV --> ROOTS : reads and writes (D5)
SRV --> HOME : reads its own files
FF --> SRV : HTTP, on the loopback
ED --> SRV : HTTP, on the loopback
SRV -.-> NET : three dictionary requests\nand nothing else (S-10)
FF -.-> NET : the extension's requests\nonly for those hosts (S-2)

note bottom of SRV
  Bound to the loopback (P-1).
  Everything it serves is on this machine.
end note

note bottom of NET
  A page in the browser can reach
  127.0.0.1 — which is why a write
  needs the token (ADR-0008).
end note
@enduml
